   },
   {
    "i": 28,
    "t0": 33.087,
    "t1": 35.537,
    "path": "out/narration/line_28.wav",
    "text": "And one win can't tell you which kind you've found.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      33.087,
      35.537
     ]
    ]
   }
  ],
  "need": 36.74
 },
 "heat": {
  "lines": [
   {
    "i": 29,
    "t0": 0.5,
    "t1": 7.9,
    "path": "out/narration/line_29.wav",
    "text": "Now let's make the start perfect, exact to the last atom, and change just one thing: the temperature of the board.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      0.5,
      4.12
     ],
     [
      4.42,
      5.94
     ],
     [
      6.34,
      7.9
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 30,
    "t0": 8.6,
    "t1": 11.67,
    "path": "out/narration/line_30.wav",
    "text": "Where would the heat come from? The chips themselves.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      8.6,
      10.02
     ],
     [
      10.42,
      11.67
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 31,
    "t0": 12.27,
    "t1": 26.274,
    "path": "out/narration/line_31.wav",
    "text": "At the top, a chip holds about five joules of energy, just from its height. As it falls, that becomes speed. And every time it hits a pin, some of that speed turns into heat: in the pin, the board, and the chip.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      12.27,
      16.914
     ],
     [
      17.214,
      19.614
     ],
     [
      19.914,
      23.714
     ],
     [
      23.914,
      26.274
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 32,
    "t0": 26.874,
    "t1": 29.916,
    "path": "out/narration/line_32.wav",
    "text": "When it stops, all five joules have become heat.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      26.874,
      27.676
     ],
     [
      27.876,
      29.916
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 33,
    "t0": 30.716,
    "t1": 44.128,
    "path": "out/narration/line_33.wav",
    "text": "Spread through the board, that warms it by less than a ten-thousandth of a degree. But warm wood and steel expand. The board grows by about a nanometre, the width of ten atoms, and every pin shifts with it.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      30.716,
      35.081
     ],
     [
      35.481,
      37.681
     ],
     [
      37.981,
      40.131
     ],
     [
      40.331,
      41.797
     ],
     [
      42.097,
      44.127
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 34,
    "t0": 44.928,
    "t1": 52.551,
    "path": "out/narration/line_34.wav",
    "text": "A nanometre is nothing, until the bounces double it, about twenty times over. Then it's a centimetre: a different slot.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      44.928,
      46.441
     ],
     [
      46.741,
      49.561
     ],
     [
